    <string name="stats_help_trend">Trend</string>
    <string name="stats_help_trend_body">The Trend tab plots any measure as a curve over time. Pick the measure with the buttons, and whether each series becomes a point or the series are merged per day, week or month (the measure is then computed over all series in the period). Per caliber draws one curve per caliber. The filters above apply to both tabs. Tap a point to read it.</string>

    <!-- Help: shared by every screen’s (?) dialog -->
    <string name="help">Help</string>
    <string name="help_close">Close</string>

    <!-- Help: home screen -->
    <string name="help_home_title">About Markera</string>
    <string name="help_home_how">How it works</string>
    <string name="help_home_how_body">Photograph a precision target and Markera finds the hits, the rings and the centre and scores the series.</string>
    <string name="help_home_marking">Mark</string>
    <string name="help_home_marking_body">Opens the camera. Point it at the target and tap to scan.</string>
    <string name="help_home_history">History</string>
    <string name="help_home_history_body">Every saved series with photo, caliber and score.</string>
    <string name="help_home_stats">Statistics</string>
    <string name="help_home_stats_body">Shot pattern and measures over time, filtered by caliber and date.</string>
    <string name="help_home_account">Account</string>
    <string name="help_home_account_body">Sign in with Google to save series. The series are stored on Markera\’s server and can be deleted at any time with Delete account.</string>

    <!-- Help: scan screen -->
    <string name="help_scan_title">How to scan</string>
    <string name="help_scan_scan">Scan</string>
    <string name="help_scan_scan_body">Fill the frame with the target and tap Detect. Markera finds the hits, the rings and the centre and scores them.</string>
    <string name="help_scan_edit">Adjust hits</string>
    <string name="help_scan_edit_body">Tap a missed hit in the photo to add it. Drag a hit to move it. Long-press a hit to remove it — you confirm first. Pinch to zoom.</string>
    <string name="help_scan_score">Score</string>
    <string name="help_scan_score_body">The score comes from where the hit sits on the target. If the hit is in the right place but the score is slightly off, tap the score box and pick the right score — the hit stays where it is. If you move the hit, the score is recalculated from its new position.</string>
    <string name="help_scan_caliber">Caliber</string>
    <string name="help_scan_caliber_body">The chip beside the score shows the caliber the series is saved with. Tap it to change — if none is chosen, the app asks when you save. The caliber is shown in the history and can be filtered on in the statistics.</string>
    <string name="help_scan_save">Save</string>
    <string name="help_scan_save_body">Saves the series with its photo to your account. You need to be signed in. The ↻ button discards the scan without saving.</string>
    <string name="help_scan_debug">Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="help_scan_debug_body">Show detection data in the menu shows the detector\’s raw boxes, digit rows and lines, plus the fitted ring and the centre.</string>

    <!-- Help: history -->
    <string name="help_history_title">About the history</string>
    <string name="help_history_list">The list</string>
    <string name="help_history_list_body">Each row is a saved series: photo, time, caliber, score and the hits. The series are grouped per day, newest first — tap a day header to unfold that day\’s series. The chips above the list filter on caliber and date, and the choice is remembered for next time.</string>
    <string name="help_history_detail">Details</string>
    <string name="help_history_detail_body">Tap a series to see it large, adjust hits or remove it. Long-press a row to delete it right away.</string>
    <string name="help_history_export">Export</string>
    <string name="help_history_export_body">Export in the menu packs the series the filter shows into a zip: series.csv and holes.csv (open in Excel) plus the saved photos.</string>
    <string name="help_history_offline">Offline</string>
    <string name="help_history_offline_body">The list and the photos stay on the phone and are shown without a connection too.</string>

    <!-- Help: series detail -->
    <string name="help_detail_title">About the series</string>
    <string name="help_detail_photo">The photo</string>
    <string name="help_detail_photo_body">The scanned target with hits, ring and centre. Pinch to zoom, drag a hit to move it and tap the target to add a missing one — the score is recalculated from the hit\’s position.</string>
    <string name="help_detail_holes">The hits</string>
    <string name="help_detail_holes_body">The list shows the ring, the distance from the centre in millimetres and whether the hit was detected or added by hand. The bin in the row removes the hit after a confirmation. Changes are saved at once; undo them from the message at the bottom.</string>
    <string name="help_detail_delete">Delete</string>
    <string name="help_detail_delete_body">Delete in the menu removes the series from the app. The server keeps the series, its hits and the target photo until you delete the account.</string>

    <!-- Statistics: help dialog -->
    <string name="stats_help">About the measures</string>
    <string name="stats_help_series">Number of series the filter (caliber and date) lets through. Only series with a saved shot pattern can be drawn and counted.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_hits">Total number of hits in those series.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_mean_distance">The distance from the target centre to each hit, in millimetres, averaged over all hits.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_mean_pairwise">The distance between every pair of hits within a series, averaged — and then averaged over the series. Series with a single hit are skipped.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_group_size">The largest distance between two hits in a series (the spread), averaged over the series.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_mean_radius">The mean distance from the hits to the series\’ own centre point (the centre of the shot pattern), averaged over the series. Measures how tight the series is regardless of where on the target it sits. Series with a single hit are skipped.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_radial_sd">The standard deviation of all selected hits\’ distances to their common centre point, in millimetres. Low value = the hits are tight, wherever on the target.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_impact">The centre of the shot pattern: the mean of all hits\’ x and y, in millimetres right of and below the centre (negative numbers mean left and up). Drawn as a + on the target.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_impact_median">The median of all hits\’ x and y separately — less sensitive to the odd flyer than the mean point. Drawn as a × on the target.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_mean_score">The mean of the series\’ total scores.</string>
    <string name="stats_help_colours">The colour scale</string>
    <string name="stats_help_colours_body">Hits are coloured by when the series was shot: the scale under the target runs from the oldest series on the left to the newest on the right. The dots on the scale show each series, and the two knobs narrow the target and the measures down to a selection of them.</string>

